//CTP Editor Structure file for EndGameObjects by Martin Gühmann
//Spelling corrections & other small changes, updated by JB
//For more detailed comments see advance.ces

0.3 //Version number

#%047%047	//Comment charachter in data file
%032%009	//Delimiter charachters in data file
		// (use %nnn for ASCII ref)
:		//Break on right quasi-delimiter
}{		//Break on left quasi-delimiter

1 //Format

f //Whether this has a number at the top (num of entries)
f //Whether this has a tree structure
f //Whether this file references GL entries
f //Whether this file has entries in gl_str.txt
f //Whether this file is the GL icon file
f //Whether this structure file describes formatting of fields
  // (i.e. whether it has the LBF and LAF columns below)

//Name				Comp	PByDef	AMult	NumArgs
	//Type			DefaultValue	Comment
Wonder				f	f	f	1
	wonder.ces		WONDER_		Wonder that should be needed to complete the endgame.  Actually I finished it without the wonder and the game crashes after the activation of the gaia controller sequence when the wonder was build.
Building			f	f	f	1
	buildings.ces		IMPROVE_	City building you need to activate the endgame.
TerrainImprovement		f	f	f	1
	tileimp.ces		TILEIMP_	Terrain improvement you need to activate the endgame.
MinNeeded			f	f	f	1
	0			10		Minimum of buildings or terrain improvements needed to activate the endgame.
MaxNeeded			f	f	f	1
	0			20		Maximum number of buildings of the end game that can be build.
IsSatellite			f	f	f	0	Is it a Satellite?  Not used in default EndGameObjects
PowerSource			f	f	f	1
	EndGameObjects.ces	ENDGAME_	The power source from this file for the terrain improvements to increase their coverrage.
MinRadius			f	f	f	1
	0			5		Minimum coverrage radius of the tile improvements.
MaxRadius			f	f	f	1
	0			8		Maximum coverrage radius of the tile improvements.
MinCoverage			f	f	f	1
	0			0.6		Minum map coverrage in order to launch the end game.
TurnsToActivate			f	f	f	1
	0			10		The number of turns to activation of the endgame from launch.
@ //End of fields
